                                "example_id": "3faeea12-efa7-433f-a015-2d8ee214f96e",
                                "sense_id": "bb3ada4f-f5f8-3c68-b9ef-7a26649fe012",
                                "text": "He scoured Florence looking at coopers with their heavy wooden hammers, the wool dyers with their arms stained blue and green, the ironmongers, blacksmiths, rustic stone bevelers working the Strozzi palace […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e536bdea-71f2-426c-af8e-0ad7d08232e1",
                                "sense_id": "bb3ada4f-f5f8-3c68-b9ef-7a26649fe012",
                                "text": "The bevelers of early America often affixed a highly individualized “beveler’s mark” to their finished products."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3e832d56-595d-4ba0-86e2-96cd199566d1",
                                "sense_id": "bb3ada4f-f5f8-3c68-b9ef-7a26649fe012",
                                "text": "There were doorbells of moribund trades, a glass beveller, a “Church and Legal” printer."
